{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "c9e5aba3-fa6f-5602-babc-574c64d96725",
		"name": "Ch 10 - Practice API Collection",
		"description": "# Practice API: sample collection\n\nA small, well-organized collection for the QAMadeEasy practice API. Use it as a model for your own collections.\n\n## Before you run\n1. Start the practice API: `node server.js` (base URL http://localhost:3000).\n2. Select the environment **Practice API - Local**.\n\n## How it is organized\n| Folder | What it covers | Auth |\n|---|---|---|\n| Users | Read users | none |\n| Products | Read products | none |\n| Reports | Sales report | API key, set once on the folder |\n\n## Variables\n- `baseUrl` comes from the environment.\n- `userId` and `productId` are collection variables (Variables tab).",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Users",
			"description": "Read-only user requests. No login needed.",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "List users",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users?limit=3",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"users"
							],
							"query": [
								{
									"key": "limit",
									"value": "3"
								}
							]
						},
						"description": "First page, three users per page."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Get one user",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"users",
								"{{userId}}"
							]
						},
						"description": "Reads the user whose id is in the collection variable `userId`.\n\n**Expected:** `200 OK` with the user. An unknown id gives `404` (see the saved examples)."
					},
					"response": [
